[s0l0!-header][h1]Animations[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

The following code defines a timer that calls the [b]move[/b]() function every 10 milliseconds:
[code format="js" ]var t = setInterval(move, 10);[/code]
However, this makes our box move to the right forever. To stop the animation when the box reaches the end of the container, we add a simple check to the move() function and use the [b]clearInterval[/b]() method to stop the timer.[code format="js" ]function move() {
  if(pos >= 150) {
    [b]clearInterval(t);[/b]
  }
  else {
    pos += 1;
    box.style.left = pos+"px";
  }
}[/code]
When the left attribute of the box reaches the value of 150, the box reaches the end of the container, based on a container width of 200 and a box width of 50.
